# Prompt files
*.prompt
!intergation.prompt

# Build artifacts
cache/
out/

# Review packs for partners (produced by build_pack.sh; not for git)
dist/

# Doc / code bundles for partners (ad-hoc zip / tar archives produced
# out-of-band to ship selected docs + reference sources via messenger;
# the canonical source always lives under docs/ and crates/). Patterns
# are anchored to the repo root so any top-level
# `<topic>_for_<recipient>_*.{zip,tar.gz,sha256}` is auto-ignored.
/*_for_*.zip
/*_for_*.tar.gz
/*_for_*.sha256

# Local cargo-audit snapshot (regenerated on demand; CI runs `cargo audit`
# fresh via the security:rust:audit job — the file in the workspace root is
# a developer convenience artefact, not a checked-in dependency).
cargo.audit

# Generated verifier and deployment artifacts
contracts/DepositVerifier.*
deployment_addresses.json
contracts/ethereum/deployment_real.json
deposit-prover/deposit_proof_output.json

# R15 / M2 bridge-evm-aggregator standalone workspace. Its Cargo.lock is
# committed because `aggregate-proof` is a deployed binary; only generated
# target/SRS/output artefacts remain local.
crates/bridge-evm-aggregator/target/
crates/bridge-evm-aggregator/params/
crates/bridge-evm-aggregator/out/

# Local-only scratch / backup artefacts (editor backups, ad-hoc patches,
# generated binaries, and not-for-commit experiments). Only USER_GUIDE.md and
# SUMMARY.md are intended to be committed from this batch.
FIX_TASK_FOR_AGENT.md.bak.*
acki-nacki_deposit-rlc-e2e.patch
deposit-prover/Cargo.lock.pse-backup
deposit-prover/Cargo.toml.bak_*
deposit-prover/Cargo.toml.pse-backup
deposit-prover/deposit_public_inputs.bin
deposit-prover/deposit_eth_circuit_params.json
deposit-prover/src/bin/an_rlc_verify.rs
docs/**/Acki_Nacki_Bridge_User_Guide.pdf.bak.*
docs/**/USER_GUIDE.pdf
docs/**/USER_GUIDE.md.bak.*

# Partner handoff / outreach messages — local-only drafts, not for commit.
docs/partner_handoff_*.md

.temp/*

# Runtime state + debug artefacts emitted by the relayer / prover binaries.
# Never commit — the .stale_* variants are ad-hoc backups from crash-recovery
# sessions; the submissions/ and diag/ dirs are env-gated dumps for offline
# replay (BRIDGE_DUMP_SUBMISSIONS_DIR, BRIDGE_DIAG_INSTANCES_FILE); the top
# `proofs/` dir is halo2 proof output. Mirrors the existing
# `crates/bridge-snark-utils/proofs/` rule.
/proofs/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/relayer-state.json
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/relayer-state.json.stale_*
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/state.stale_*/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/submissions/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/diag/

# Prover SRS / vk / pk artefacts — ~40 GB total, regenerated on demand
# by keygen (~7 min per circuit). Shared between the bundle daemon and
# the withdraw-e2e CLI (`BRIDGE_PARAMS_DIR` / `--params-dir`). Mirrors
# `crates/bridge-snark-utils/params/*.srs` and
# `crates/bridge-evm-aggregator/params/`.
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/params/

# Per-mode config dirs (L1_config/, L2_config/) — the runtime subdirs
# hold live prover state, proofs, and scratch witnesses, never commit.
# The `env` files and `shellnet.common` are tracked development fixtures.
# Production runtime envs and keys live outside the repository.
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L1_config/relayer-state.json*
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L1_config/state/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L1_config/state.pre_deploy_*/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L1_config/proofs/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L1_config/work_dir/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L2_config/relayer-state.json*
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L2_config/state/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L2_config/state.pre_deploy_*/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L2_config/proofs/
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/L2_config/work_dir/

# CLI smoke-test runtime dirs (created by scripts/local_smoke.sh,
# scripts/live_smoke.sh, scripts/deploy_msig_and_mint.{sh,py} when
# invoked from the CLI crate root). Contain multisig keys.json,
# per-withdrawal idempotency state, aggregate-proof scratch, and logs.
crates/ackinacki-bridge/work_dir/
crates/ackinacki-bridge/withdraw-state/

# Per-user output artifacts from scripts/deploy_msig_and_mint.{sh,py}
# — the eval-able env line + stdout/stderr captures. Contain absolute
# local paths and per-run multisig addresses; not source-of-truth.
crates/ackinacki-bridge/deploy_msig*.env
crates/ackinacki-bridge/deploy_msig*.log

# Aggregator scratch dir if a user runs the CLI without setting
# BRIDGE_SNARK_DIR (falls back to args.rs default `./shplonk-snark`).
# The profile files point at ./work_dir/shplonk-snark instead, but this
# catches the direct-invocation case.
crates/ackinacki-bridge/shplonk-snark/

# tvm-cli is platform-specific; each operator supplies their own on PATH
# or via CLI_NAME. A committed binary silently shadows the working one,
# because deploy_msig_and_mint.py prepends this directory to PATH.
crates/bridge-prover-libraries/python/bin/tvm-cli

# tvm-cli rewrites this file with a machine-local absolute path on every
# run, so a committed copy makes every operator's tree dirty.
crates/ackinacki-bridge/tvm-cli.conf.json
